Day 2 ✅
Warm Up: P2 
Race 1: P8 
-
A strong Saturday here in Aragon! After yesterday’s qualifying, I was confident to redeem myself in the race today. A strong warm up gave me some great confidence going into the first race laps of the weekend. 
-
Starting P19 on the grid, I rode hard to make up 10 places in 4 laps and the front group only 0.5 seconds up the road, until the red flag came out. However, this meant I lined up P9 for the restart, with the sole goal of fighting and learning in the front group, and that’s exactly what we did! 
-
The laps at the front were good, I tried to push my way up as far as I could, but ultimately learnt for my race tomorrow. 
-
Fantastic job to my PHR Team, we start P8 again for race 2 💪🏻
